 `Collapsible` sections inside Accordion. Give each section a stable, unique `id`.\nSee the Collapsible component documentation for more information about section anatomy, panel content, and trigger styling."},"54":{"id":"/docs/components/accordion-30","page_id":"/docs/components/accordion","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/accordion#customization","content":"Use `defaultExpandedKeys` for initial expansion, or `expandedKeys` with `onExpandedChange` for\ncontrolled state. Keys must match the section IDs; the callback receives a `Set` of expanded keys.\nBy default, only one section can stay open. Set `allowsMultipleExpanded` to keep several open.\nBoth behaviors are shown in the examples."},"55":{"id":"/docs/components/accordion-31","page_id":"/docs/components/accordion","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/accordion#customization","content":"Use `className` and `style` to customize the group container. `data-disabled` reflects the group's\ndisabled state. Customize individual headings, triggers, and panels on the composed Collapsible sections."},"56":{"id":"/docs/components/accordion-32","page_id":"/docs/components/accordion","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/accordion#keyboard","content":"Key"},"57":{"id":"/docs/components/accordion-33","page_id":"/docs/components/accordion","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/accordion#keyboard","content":"Action"},"58":{"id":"/docs/components/accordion-34","page_id":"/docs/components/accordion","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/accordion#keyboard","content":"`Tab` / `Shift + Tab`"},"59":{"id":"/docs/components/accordion-35","page_id":"/docs/components/accordion","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/accordion#keyboard","content":"Move between enabled triggers and controls in expanded panels"},"60":{"id":"/docs/components/accordion-36","page_id":"/docs/components/accordion","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/accordion#keyboard","content":"`Enter` / `Space`"},"61":{"id":"/docs/components/accordion-37","page_id":"/docs/components/accordion","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/accordion#keyboard","content":"Toggle the focused section; focus stays on the trigger"},"62":{"id":"/docs/components/accordion-38","page_id":"/docs/components/accordion","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/accordion#aria","content":"Each section's trigger is a native button with `aria-expanded` and `aria-controls` linked to its panel."},"63":{"id":"/docs/components/accordion-39","page_id":"/docs/components/accordion","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/accordion#aria","content":"Each panel is labeled by its trigger through `aria-labelledby` automatically."},"64":{"id":"/docs/components/accordion-40","page_id":"/docs/components/accordion","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/accordion#best-practices","content":"Group related sections and keep essential information visible outside the accordion."},"65":{"id":"/docs/components/accordion-41","page_id":"/docs/components/accordion","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/accordion#best-practices","content":"Use descriptive section titles and heading levels that fit the page hierarchy."},"66":{"id":"/docs/components/accordion-42","page_id":"/docs/components/accordion","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/accordion#best-practices","content":"Use multiple expansion when users need to compare information across sections."},"67":{"id":"/docs/components/accordion-43","page_id":"/docs/components/accordion","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/accordion#best-practices","content":"Keep item IDs stable when reordering or filtering data."},"68":{"id":"/docs/components/accordion-44","page_id":"/docs/components/accordion","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/accordion#best-practices","content":"Manage expansion on Accordion when sections belong to a group."},"69":{"id":"/docs/components/accordion-45","page_id":"/docs/components/accordion","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/accordion#best-practices","content":"Keep form validation and step progression in application logic."},"70":{"id":"/docs/components/accordion-46","page_id":"/docs/components/accordion","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/accordion#controlled-state-not-updating","content":"Update `expandedKeys` from `onExpandedChange` and make sure the keys match the item IDs.\nChanging `defaultExpandedKeys` after mounting does not control expansion."},"71":{"id":"/docs/components/accordion-47","page_id":"/docs/components/accordion","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/accordion#sections-close-when-another-opens","content":"Enable `allowsMultipleExpanded` when several sections should remain open together.\nFor a single independent section, use Collapsible without an Accordion."},"72":{"id":"/docs/components/alert","page_id":"/docs/components/alert","type":"page","content":"Alert","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Components"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/alert"},"73":{"id":"/docs/components/alert-0","page_id":"/docs/components/alert","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/alert","content":"In-page alerts are non-intrusive notifications within a webpage, providing users with timely information or feedback without disrupting their experience."},"74":{"id":"/docs/components/alert-1","page_id":"/docs/components/alert","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/alert#installation","content":"Installation"},"75":{"id":"/docs/components/alert-2","page_id":"/docs/components/alert","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/alert#examples","content":"Examples"},"76":{"id":"/docs/components/alert-3","page_id":"/docs/components/alert","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/alert#default","content":"Default"},"77":{"id":"/docs/components/alert-4","page_id":"/docs/components/alert","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/alert#emphasis-variants","content":"Emphasis